# The 3D food: the frame, the registry, the kit (world lane, 2026-11-08)

What a food agent needs to draw a restaurant, and what the page agent calls from game.js. Code: `js/world.js` (the
frame), `js/food/kit.js` (the registry `BB.food` and the kit `k`), `js/food/diner.js` (the worked example).
Tests: `tests/food.test.cjs`. Spec: FOODCOURT-BUILD.md 5.2 and 6.5.

## 1. Files and load order

index.html, right after `js/vendor/three.min.js`, in the marked block:

```html
<!-- world: ... -->
<script src="js/food/kit.js"></script>      <!-- BB.food: the registry, the kit, the kit's own module -->
<script src="js/food/diner.js"></script>    <!-- each restaurant's food module, one line each -->
<!-- /world -->
```

A food module loads before the packs and the core; it registers a factory and touches nothing else until a pack
uses it. **Food agents: ask the page agent to add your `js/food/<pack>.js` line to that block** (index.html is
the page's). Every module file is UMD like js/core, so Node loads it: copy diner.js's first five and last two lines.

## 2. The world, as game.js calls it (page lane, phase 2)

| Call | What it does |
|---|---|
| `BB.world.init()` | renderer, scene, camera; builds the active pack's sets (the diner until `usePack`) |
| `BB.world.usePack(pack)` (alias `use`) | the restaurant whose food is drawn; frees the old sets, builds the new ones, keeps the current scene |
| `BB.world.goTo(name)` | a station id, a backdrop name, `'counter'`, or `null` (the court: no 3D). stage.setScene already calls it |
| `BB.world.showStep(q, made)` | what a station shows for a step: `q` = `BB.shift.question()`, `made` = `BB.line.made(pack, order, q.item)`. Returns a Promise (the slide-in) |
| `BB.world.outcome(e, made, opts)` | one playout event from `BB.shift.answer()`, `made` = the item after it. Resolves when it has played. `opts.onApply()` is called as the food goes on (play its sound then); `opts.ms` = Simple cooking's length (1800, Timed 700) |
| `BB.world.cookStage(e)` | the Timed clock's `stage` event (or a stage index): the food on the heat shows that stage |
| `BB.world.showCounter(list)` | the review: `list` = `[made()]`, one per item |
| `BB.world.serveOut()` | the order slides to the customer (Promise) |
| `BB.world.colourOf(ing, k)`, `marksOf(ing, k)` | the dial plate's swatch and mark count for stage index k |
| `BB.world.graphics` | the NarbeGraphics handle (`openGame('bensfoodcourt')`) for the `graphics-quality` row: `label()`, `cycle()`, `setChoice()`; null without the hub module |
| `BB.world.at`, `.set`, `.pack` | the name goTo was given; the set on show; the pack |

`outcome` understands `added, skipped, swapped, picked, cooked, phaseDone, auto`; every other event resolves at once.
What happens: an Add of something that cooks drops onto the heat; any other Add goes on the item (the module's line
handler, e.g. the squirt); Skip slides it away; Swap tosses it; a pick of something that cooks drops into the
basket; any other pick re-draws the item with a little bounce (or the set's own `pick` hook); `cooked` runs the
cook's flourish when the heat is on show; `phaseDone` drops a `builds.cap` (the top bun) on; `auto` plays the
module's flourish named by `e.show`.

**Kept until game.js switches over** (they work exactly as before): `showGrill(ing, n, stage)`,
`dropOnGrill(ing, n)`, `cookGrill(stage, ms)`, `grillStage(stage)`, `showBoard(parts, incoming)`,
`lineOutcome(kind, { onSquirt })`, `showCounter`, `serveOut`, `colourOf`, `__scene()`. dom-play.cjs reads the
object named `'incoming'` and its `userData.bottle`; review-frames.cjs reads `userData.sauce.geo`: both kept.

## 3. A food module

```js
BB.food.register('<pack>', k => ({
  uses: ['diner'],                 // optional: borrow another module's shapes, sets, cooks (searched after yours)
  shapes:   { <look.shape>: (part, o) => ({ g, h }) },
  sets:     { <backdrop name>: { cam, line, surface, build, cook?, pick?, finish?, auto?, x?, picture? } },
  layouts:  { <name>: (made, o) => ({ g, h, ... }) },
  layoutOf: made => '<layout name>' | null,          // null: 'stack'
  cooks:    { <name>: { show(c, s), add?(c, s), run?(c, s), stage?(c, s) } },
  lines:    { <apply>: { incoming?(part, c), add?(c), skip?(c), swap?(c) } },
  applies:  { <look.shape>: '<apply>' },             // which line handler a shape uses; look.apply wins
  autos:    { <show>: (c, e, made) => Promise },     // flourishes of auto steps
  fx:       { <fx key>: (g, value, box, c) => {} },  // gross-out fx beyond the kit's
  ramps:    { <look.shape>: [colour by stage] },     // the dial plates' swatches (world.colourOf)
  counter:  { arrange(n, list, anchors) -> [{ p, s }] | null },
}));
```

Every section is optional. Lookups go: your module, then what it `uses`, then `'kit'`. **A pack with no module yet
borrows the diner's**, so it still draws something; tests/food.test.cjs marks it TODO until `js/food/<pack>.js`
exists, then holds it to every check. The pack id is the module id (or `pack.world.module`; schema ignores `world`).

**Rules** (tests/food.test.cjs checks each):
- Deterministic: no `Math.random`. Use `k.rand(seed)` with a seed from the part (`part.ing + ':' + part.n`).
- Bodies are `k.toon()` (MeshToon) or `k.basic()`/MeshBasic. Only ink hulls (`k.ink`, `k.inkThin`, `k.inkInstanced`)
  use a ShaderMaterial; the review renderer hides those. Sprites are invisible in review frames: use meshes.
- Many small pieces (seeds, sprinkles, rice, ice) go in one `k.scatter`/`k.heap` (InstancedMesh), not a mesh each.
- A partly drawn thing (a pour, a bead) uses `geometry.setDrawRange` on an indexed geometry, or a rebuild.
- Never build at load time and never capture the pack in the factory: call `k.pack()` when you build.

### 3.1 Shapes: one builder per `look.shape`

`(part, o) => ({ g, h })`. `g` is a `THREE.Group` standing on y = 0, centred on x = z = 0; `h` (>= 0) is where the
next part stacks. `part = { ing, done?, layer?, flavour?, gross?, n, look?, slot?, pick? }`: `n` is its place in the
stack (seed rotations with it); a slot value comes with its own `look`. Read the look with `k.lookFor(part)` (never
`pack.ingredients[...]` directly: a slot value has no ingredient). `o`:

| o | |
|---|---|
| `stage` | a stage index to draw (the cook view and the dial); without it, `k.stageIndex(part, o)` reads `part.done` |
| `item` | the whole `made()` (a cup reads `o.item.size`) |
| `below()`, `base` | the box of what is under it (stack coordinates) and the height it sits at: toppings land on it |
| `growing` | a bead being squirted: give it its own geometry copy |
| `giant` | the item's giant scale (the world already scales the item; read it only to change detail) |
| `where` | `'line'`, `'counter'` |

Gross-out fx are added by the kit after your builder runs: don't add them yourself.

### 3.2 Sets: one per backdrop name, cameras solved to the surface line

```js
grill: {
  x: -12,                                   // optional; sets are spaced 12 apart when left out
  cam: { pos: [x, y, z], at: [x, y, z], fov },   // set-local; the look of the food (keep food low, left of centre)
  line: 0.64,                               // where the backdrop's painted surface starts, fraction down the picture
  surface: { y: 0.5, back: -0.3 },          // your 3D work surface's top and back edge (z): what goes on the line
  build(g, k) { /* furniture into g */ return anchors; },
  cook: 'grill',                            // a key of cooks: this set has food on the heat
},
```

World.js shifts the camera's lens vertically (a view offset, so the food's look never changes) until
`surface.back` lands on `line` **for the window's own shape**: the backdrop is drawn with `cover`, so on a 16:9
screen a 64% line is at 66.6% of the screen, on 4:3 at 64%. `line: null` fixes the camera to the screen instead
(the counters: see below). **Measure your pictures**: the generated ones miss the prompt's line by up to 2%. The
diner's, measured from art-source/backdrops (the row where the wall's ink line ends):

| backdrop | 5.2 table | measured, used |
|---|---|---|
| grill | 65 | 64.0 |
| board | 62 | 64.0 |
| fryer (diner-fryer) | 65 | 65.7 (the fryer's back rim) |
| drinks (diner-drinks) | 62 | 63.2 (the red counter) |
| counter (every restaurant) | 78 | 80 (revised 2026-11-09, see below) |

**Counters (REVISED 2026-11-09, spec 5.2; this replaces the phase-1 rule below it).** The user found the Burger
Bar's counter too high: it covered the painted queue and pushed the served customer far up the screen. Every counter
set is now solved to its picture like a station: `line: 0.80` (one value for every restaurant) and `surface: { y:
<counter top>, back: <its back edge z> }`, so the counter top's back edge lands at 80% of the picture (about 85.5% of
a 16:9 screen). The page reads that line's screen position from `BB.world` and places the served customer (hips at
the counter, eyes near the painted horizon), the bubble and the counter props from it; the order on the counter sits
on the counter top, fully on screen.

*Superseded phase-1 rule, kept for the record:* the customer was placed by CSS the same way in every restaurant (88vh
tall, feet at 91vh) and the 3D counter hid their legs, so the diner's counter top started at 54.7% of the screen with
`line: null` and `cam: { pos: [0, 1.75, 3.6], at: [0, 1.05, -0.4], fov: 42 }`, top at y 0.92.

**Anchors** (`build()` returns them; set-local Vector3s and numbers):

| anchor | for |
|---|---|
| `stack` | where the item stands (line sets) |
| `incoming` | where an Add's ingredient waits; it slides in from 1.4 to the right |
| `surface` | the work surface's y (a line handler's `rest` sits on it) |
| `vesselScale` [x, y, z], `contentScale` | shrink the vessel (the board's plate) or the food on it (the counter) |
| `giantMax` | cap a giant item on this line set (the board: 1.2) |
| `spots`, `row`, `front`, `minX`, `maxX` | counters: one item's spot; the depth more items sit at; keep items in front of `front` and between `minX`..`maxX` |
| anything else | your cook's (`slots` for the grill, `basket`, `oil` for the fryer, `tap` for the drinks) |

Set hooks (optional): `pick(c, e, made)` a pick on this set (the drinks: a size drops the cup in, a drink pours),
`finish(c, e, made)` the phase is done, `auto(c, e, made)` a flourish here. Each returns a Promise.

### 3.3 Assembly from made()

`made()` (docs/api/line.md 3) is `{ recipe, ing, size?, done?, parts: [{ ing, done?, layer?, flavour?, gross? }],
gross, picks, counts, auto }`. The world draws an item with `k.item(made, o)`: your `layoutOf(made)` names the
layout (default `'stack'`), the layout builds it, then a giant item is scaled up.

`k.sequence(made, o)` -> `{ vessel, body, parts }` puts it in line order for you:
- **vessel**: `made.ing` when a station of the recipe `builds.on` it (the plate, the cup);
- **body**: otherwise `made.ing` itself, at `made.done` (the fries);
- **parts**: `made.parts` in order, with every **slot pick that has a look** (`pack.slots.<slot>.values[].look`)
  inserted where its step falls in the line (crust, sauce, then cheese), a repeat as one part per pick in pick order
  (two vanilla scoops are two parts); a pick's gross-out (`made.gross` `{ slot, value, event }`) is kept on its part.
  `o.hide: ['top']` leaves the cap off.

The kit's `stack` layout stacks vessel, body, parts. Write your own when food goes *in* or *round* something: the
diner's `cup` (the drink fills the cup, ice floats, a straw once poured; `o.level` 0..1 and `setLevel(t)` for the
pour) and `boat` (fried food in a paper boat). Read `made.picks`, `made.counts` (repeats) and `made.auto` (flourishes
that ran: draw the burrito wrapped once `wrap` is in it). A layout returns `{ g, h }`, plus `stack` (the group a
bead lands on) when it has one; `giantDone: true` if it scaled itself.

### 3.4 Cooking visuals, per stage

`set.cook` names a `cooks` entry. The world keeps the state `s = { ing, n, stage, cooking, timed, set, made }`:

| hook | when | must |
|---|---|---|
| `show(c, s)` | every redraw (c.F is already empty) | draw `n` of `ing` (or `made`, for a whole item) at stage index `s.stage`; `s.cooking` true while Timed cooks it |
| `add(c, s)` | an Add of it, or a pick of what cooks | `c.redraw({ ing, n })`, then animate the newest in; resolve |
| `run(c, s)` | Simple's answer (`s.stage`, `s.ms`) | a flourish that ends showing `s.stage` |
| `stage(c, s)` | each Timed stage | default `c.redraw({ stage })` |

`c = { k, F (the food group), fx (a layer redraws leave alone: steam), anchors, state, redraw(s) }`. The cook view is
used for a cook step, an Add of an ingredient with `stages`, and a pick whose values cook; a cook step that names
its own set (`stages`, `q.set`) gets it in `s.set`. **Doneness must show as a colour and a mark** (DESIGN.md); a
`look.ramp` (array by stage, or `{ stageName: colour }`) or your module's `ramps` gives the dial its swatches.

### 3.5 The line: incoming and outcomes (add, skip, swap, pick, auto)

On an Add the world puts the ingredient on the `incoming` anchor (`k.food(part)`, gross fx and all) and slides it
in; Add arcs it onto the item, Skip slides it right, Swap tosses it. A shape can wait and go on its own way:
`applies: { sauce: 'squirt' }` (or `look.apply: 'squirt'` in the pack) picks `lines.squirt`:
`incoming(part, c) -> { g, h, rest? }` (`rest`: stand on the surface, this high) and `add(c)` / `skip(c)` /
`swap(c)` -> Promise. The kit has `squirt` (a squeeze bottle, then a bead across the food) and `shake` (a shaker,
then grains); the diner adds `scoop` (ice). A pick with a gross-out (spec 4.6) puts **the bad value** on the line
with its fx; picking it puts it on like an Add, Swap tosses it. `c` for lines and hooks:

`{ k, F, fx, anchors, made, item (its build), inc (the waiting group), part, stack, onApply, top() (where food
lands, in F), toF(obj, v), showItem(made, layoutOpts) -> build, drop(g, dy, ms), pop(g) }`. Call `c.onApply()` as
the food goes on. After an Add or a pick the world redraws the item from the new `made`, so animate, don't rebuild.

### 3.6 The counter

`showCounter(list)` builds each item with its layout (`where: 'counter'`) and places it with your
`counter.arrange(n, list, anchors)` -> `[{ p: Vector3, s: scale }]`, or, when that returns null, side by side
across `minX..maxX` in ticket order, each as wide as it is, shrunk together only if they don't fit. Every item is
then kept in front of `front` and inside the span. The diner keeps one item where it always sat (0.35, 0.92, 0.55).

### 3.7 Giant

An item is giant when its recipe has `giant` or `look.giant`, or its body, a part or a picked value has a
`look.giant`: `true` draws it 1.6 times bigger, a number that much. On the counter it is kept on the counter; a line
set may cap it (`giantMax`). It never adds choices.

### 3.8 Gross-out fx (`pack.gross[].fx`)

The kit applies them to any built part: `tint: colour` and `droop: true` change the food; `stink: true|colour`
(three wavy lines rising), `smoke: true|colour` (puffs rising), `hair: true|colour` (across the top), `fly: true`
(circling; sitting on top with Motion Reduced) and `spots: colour | { colour, n }` (mould, bruises, freezer burn)
are placed from the food's own box, so they sit on top of anything. Add your own keys in `fx` (`wink`, `burst`,
`as` ...): `(g, value, box, c)`; mark what you add with `k.fxPart(obj)` so boxes ignore it, and keep it at or above
`box.max.y`. They are meshes, so the review frames show them.

### 3.9 Low and Reduced

- **Low** (Graphics Quality Low, `k.low()`): world.js caps the canvas (NarbeGraphics) and, on a change, rebuilds
  what is on show. Thin decoration only: `k.thin(n, min)` (counts: seeds, grains, sprinkles, bubbles) and
  `k.seg(n)` (radial segments). **Never thin a cue**: doneness marks, char, a gross-out, the pieces that show an
  ingredient is there (ice: at least 4 cubes).
- **Reduced** (`k.reduced()`): `k.tween(ms, fn)` calls `fn(1)` at once and `k.wait()` resolves at once, so write
  every animation with them and it resolves by itself. Things that keep moving use `k.spin(obj, kind, opts)`
  (`rise`, `orbit`, `bubble`, `bob`, `spinY`; `opts.until` ms): they sit still where you placed them, so place them
  where they should rest (on top of the food).

The scene is drawn only when something changed or moves (tweens, spinners on show).

## 4. The kit `k`

| | |
|---|---|
| materials | `toon(colour, opts)` and `basic(colour, opts)` (cached: never change or dispose them); `own(mat)` (freed with the food: clones); `keep(geo)` (shared, never freed); `ink(geo, mat, noOutline)`, `inkThin`, `inkInstanced(geo, mat, matrices, { outline: false | 'thin' })`; `SHINE` |
| geometry | `cyl(r, h, seg)`, `lathe([[x, y]...], seg, scale)`, `noise(a, j)`, `rand(seed)`, `hash(str)`, `matrix(p, rot, s)`, `piece(name)` (grain cube chunk ball stick chip seed shred sprinkle leaf), `sample(surface, n, seed)` (disc rect dome ring torus box), `boxOf(obj)` |
| shared builders | `scatter(piece, mat, points, opts)`, `heap(piece, mat, { n, r, h, seed })`, `fill(profile, level, colour)`, `pour({ F, from, to(t), colour, ms, onLevel, onApply })`, `blenderJar({ base, lid, h, r })` (`inner.profile` for a fill), `bottle(part)`, `bead(part, o)` (`look.path`: zigzag spiral drizzle), `growBead`, `squirt(F, inc, stack, onApply)`, `shaker(part)`, `shake(c)`, `puff(colour, alpha)` |
| colour | `mix(a, b, t)`, `ramp(look, stage, list)`, `marks(look, stage)` |
| pack | `pack()`, `lookOf(id)`, `lookFor(part)`, `slotLook(slot, value)`, `stageList(ing, set)`, `stageIndex(part, o)` |
| building | `food(part, o)` (shape + fx), `stack(parts, o)`, `sequence(made, o)`, `item(made, o)`, `giant(made)`, `gross(g, eventId)`, `fxPart(obj)`, `find(section, name)`, `module(id)` |
| detail, motion | `low()`, `detail()`, `thin(n, min)`, `seg(n)`, `reduced()`, `ease(t)`, `tween(ms, fn)`, `wait(ms)`, `spin(obj, kind, opts)`, `dirty()` |

The kit's own module (`'kit'`) has the shapes `disc` (also any unknown look), `blob`, `scatter` (look: piece,
colour, colours, count, size), `heap` (piece, colour, count, r, h), `fill`, `bead` (look: colour, cap, path), `jar`;
the `stack` layout; lines `squirt`, `shake`; the `pop` flourish; and every fx in 3.8.

## 5. The worked example: js/food/diner.js

- **Shapes**: the burger's moved verbatim (the diner draws the same, frame for frame), plus salt, the cup, ice,
  drinks. `sauce` is the kit's bead.
- **Sets**: counter (fixed camera), grill (cook `grill`: up to 3 in `slots`), board (`stack`, `incoming`, the plate
  at 0.8, giants capped at 1.2), fryer (cook `fryer`: the oil well at the back with the wire `basket`, the
  paper-boat landing in front, a shallower camera so both fit), drinks (`tap`; its `pick` hook drops the cup in, then
  pours the drink).
- **Cooks**: `grill` (drop, sizzle-hop-flip, steam), `fryer` (drop into the basket, dunk and bubble, brown by stage,
  lift and shake).
- **Lines**: sauces squirt (kit), salt shakes (kit), ice is scooped (`scoop`).
- **Layouts**: `cup` (made.ing's look is `cup`), `boat` (body `fries` or `onionRings`); everything else `stack`.
- **Ramps**: patty raw to charred; fries and rings raw to burnt.

### Looks the diner module provides (content-diner uses only these, or files a Request)

<!-- diner-looks -->
| look.shape | draws | look fields |
|---|---|---|
| `bun` | bottom bun (crumb face); `layer: 'top'` the seeded dome | colour |
| `patty` | a patty, one grill mark per stage, char flecks when charred | (colour by stage: ramp) |
| `slice` | a draped square slice (cheese) | colour |
| `strips` | two wavy strips with a fat stripe (bacon) | colour, fat |
| `leaf` | a ruffled leaf (lettuce) | colour |
| `disc` | two round slices with a lighter face (tomato) | colour, inner |
| `chips` | four chips (pickles) | colour, inner |
| `rings` | two raw rings (onion) | colour |
| `sauce` | a squeeze-bottle bead across the food; waits in its bottle | colour, cap, path, beadScale, bottleScale |
| `plate` | the diner's blue-rimmed plate (a vessel) | |
| `fries` | 22 fries, raw to burnt by stage; in a paper boat on their own | (ramp) |
| `onionRings` | five battered rings, raw to burnt by stage | (ramp) |
| `sprinkle` | salt: fine grains over the food under it; waits in a shaker | colour, count, shakerScale |
| `cup` | a paper cup, small/medium/large by `made.size`; the drink and ice go in it | |
| `ice` | ice cubes (in the cup: a cupful, or floating on the drink); waits in a scoop | |
| `drink` | the drink filling the cup, poured from the fountain; a straw once full | colour |
<!-- /diner-looks -->

Any look may also say `giant` (3.7), `ramp` and `marks` (3.4), `apply` (3.5).

## 6. Testing and looking

- `node --test "tests/food.test.cjs"` (and `BB_PACKS=<id>`): every look resolves; every builder at every stage
  (h >= 0, ink only on hulls, deterministic); every set builds and its lens lands on the line at 16:9, 16:10, 4:3 and
  21:9; every recipe assembles at every step of its line (walked by line.js) and on the counter; the cook visuals
  draw every stage; every fx exists and sits on the food; the kit's sequence, giant, Low, Reduced and shared builders.
- Frames: `JSDOM=<jsdom> node tools/review-frames.cjs <out> [tut]`, then `python tools/review_compose.py <out>`;
  they show the diner's grill, board and counter. For your own sets, drive `BB.world` in jsdom the same way
  (usePack, goTo, showStep, outcome, showCounter) and render `BB.world.__scene()` with NARBEKART's node_render.cjs.
